                "answers_tail_for_review": [
                  "ough the space between the triangles without cutting through either triangle's interior. **(Valid)**\n    *   **C to F (Right Bottom):** The line connects the bottom corners of both triangles. This is a straight line along the bottom (or below the triangles), so it does not dissect them. **(Valid)**\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe only connections that dissect a triangle are **$A \\rightarrow E$** and **$A \\rightarrow F$**, which both cut through the interior of the Left Triangle. The other $7$ connections are valid.\n\nTotal valid ways = $9 - 2 = 7$.\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThere are **7** ways this is possible.",
                  "exterior without cutting through the interior.\n    *   Therefore, **any** straight line connecting a marked vertex on the left triangle to a marked vertex on the right triangle will pass through the gap and will not dissect either triangle.\n\n4.  **Count the combinations**:\n    *   Number of choices for the left vertex = 2.\n    *   Number of choices for the right vertex = 2.\n    *   Total number of connecting lines = $2 \\times 2 = 4$.\n\nThe four possible connections are:\n1.  Left Red $\\to$ Right Red\n2.  Left Red $\\to$ Right Blue\n3.  Left Blue $\\to$ Right Red\n4.  Left Blue $\\to$ Right Blue\n\n**4**"
                ],
