                "expected_wrong_answer": "5.5",
                "statuses": [
                  "completed",
                  "completed"
                ],
                "answers_tail_for_review": [
                  "gle is $1$, the length of the altitude of a unit triangle is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$. The base of the unit triangle is $1$. The area formula $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\text{base} \\cdot \\text{height}$ works out. In our coordinate geometry, the unit is the side length of the small triangle ($1 \\mathrm{~cm}$).\nTherefore, the area is directly **$4.75\\sqrt{3}$**.\n\nAlternatively, converting to a decimal:\n$$ 4.75\\sqrt{3} \\approx 4.75 \\times 1.732 \\approx 8.23 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2} $$\n\n**Answer:**\nThe area of the shaded triangle is **$4.75\\sqrt{3}$** $\\mathrm{cm}^{2}$ (or approximately **$8.23$** $\\mathrm{cm}^{2}$).",
                  "s located at the 5th unit mark. Coordinates: **$(5, 0)$**.\n\n**3. Calculation of the Shaded Area**\nUsing the determinant formula with vertices $P(0,1)$, $Q(4,2)$, and $R(5,0)$:\n\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(2-0) + 4(0-1) + 5(1-2) \\right| $$\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 - 4 - 5 \\right| $$\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -9 \\right| $$\n$$ \\text{Area} = 4.5 $$\n\nAlternatively, subtracting the corner triangles from the total rectangle bounding box (width 5, height 2, area 10) yields $10 - 1 - 5.5 - 5.5 + 4.5 = 4.5$.\n\nThe area of the shaded triangle is **$4.5 \\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$**."
                ],
                "note": "Answer tails are for manual inspection; no automatic final-answer success grading."
              }
            ],
            "original_controls": [],
            "independent_review": null,
            "approval_status": "No user Pass/Collect recorded"
          },
