                  "2} \\times 4 \\times 1 = 2$.\n2.  **Bottom-Right Region:** A triangle with vertices $(4,0), (5,0), (5,4)$.\n    Area = $\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 4 = 2$.\n3.  **Top-Left Region:** A triangle with vertices $(0,1), (0,4), (5,4)$.\n    Area = $\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 3 = 7.5$.\n\nFinally, subtract these from the total rectangle area:\n$\\text{Area of Shaded Triangle} = 20 - (2 + 2 + 7.5)$\n$\\text{Area} = 20 - 11.5 = 8.5$\n\n**Answer:**\nThe area of the shaded triangle is **8.5** $\\mathrm{~cm}^{2}$.",
                  "e with vertices $(x_1, y_1)$, $(x_2, y_2)$, and $(x_3, y_3)$ is given by the formula:\n    $$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} |x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2)| $$\n\n    Plugging in our coordinates:\n    *   $(x_1, y_1) = (0, 1)$\n    *   $(x_2, y_2) = (3, 3)$\n    *   $(x_3, y_3) = (4, 0)$\n\n    $$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} |0(3 - 0) + 3(0 - 1) + 4(1 - 3)| $$\n    $$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} |0 + 3(-1) + 4(-2)| $$\n    $$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} |-3 - 8| $$\n    $$ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} |-11| $$\n    $$ \\text{Area} = 5.5 $$\n\nThe area of the shaded triangle is **5.5** $\\mathrm{cm}^{2}$."
